# 2024/2025 finalize + derive backfill

The seed already carried complete 2024/2025 player_match stats (9,936 rows per
season) but left them `no_data`, unscored, with no rushed behinds and no ladder.
This backfill gave 2024/2025 the same finish as the 1998–2023 import: rushed
behinds, `data_status='final'`, `drv_score`, and `club_season` ladders.

Unlike 1998–2023 (which was scraped and inserted whole), the 2024/2025 matches
already existed in the seed — so nothing was imported. The team-behinds figures
were scraped and joined onto the existing rows.

## 1) Rushed behinds — season-page scrape

Source: team score lines on afltables.com/afl/seas/{2024,2025}.html (the same
season pages used for 1998–2023). For each team in a match the final quarter's
behinds tally is the team total; `rushed_behinds = GREATEST(0, team_behinds −
Σ player behinds)`.

Join key: `(season, round, club)` — a club plays exactly one match per round, so
this uniquely identifies a club_match and sidesteps home/away designation
(the join is on club, not side).

Two reconciliations were required and verified before any write:

- **Round labels.** afltables numbers the season `Round 1..25`; the seed uses
  `Opening Round` + `Round 1..24`. afltables `Round 1` (4 games) = seed
  `Opening Round`; afltables `Round N` = seed `Round N-1`; finals labels
  identical. Confirmed by per-round match-count fingerprint on both seasons.
- **Club names.** afltables short names (`Sydney`, `Adelaide`, …) map to the
  seed's full names (`Sydney Swans`, `Adelaide Crows`, …) by prefix; 1:1 across
  all 18 clubs.

Safety net: staged rows were resolved to club_match rows and the cardinality
checked to be an exact bijection — 864 staged rows ↔ 864 club_match rows, no
orphans on either side — before the UPDATE. (Silent mis-assignment was the
failure mode of the earlier player-stat import attempt; this check forecloses
it.)

Result (UPDATE 864):

- 2024: 962 rushed behinds, avg 2.23/team/match, max 8, 382/432 innings ≥1.
- 2025: 878 rushed behinds, avg 2.03/team/match, max 8, 375/432 innings ≥1.
  (In line with 1998–2023: avg 2.26, max 11.)

Spot check — 2024 Grand Final: Brisbane 18.12.120 → 12 behinds (rushed 3 +
player 9); Sydney 9.6.60 → 6 behinds (rushed 1 + player 5). Correct.

## 2) Finalize + derive

Reused `derive-ladders.sql` with the year range set to 2024–2025, after first
flipping the 432 matches to `data_status='final'` (the derive steps filter on
it):

- `club_match.drv_score` = Σ(goals×6 + behinds) + rushed_behinds — 864 innings.
- `club_season` ladder standings from home-and-away results only (finals
  excluded via `NOT ILIKE '%Final%'`; 2024/2025 both have finals, so unlike the
  2026 validation run this exclusion actually bites) — 36 club-seasons.

Validation — ladders match real AFL history:

- 2024: Sydney Swans minor premiers (17–6, 68 pts, 126.7%); Port Adelaide 2nd;
  Richmond wooden spoon (2–21). Premier (Brisbane) won the GF; GF excluded from
  the ladder, as it should be.
- 2025: Adelaide Crows top (18–5, 72 pts); Geelong 2nd; Brisbane 3rd carrying
  the season's one draw (16–6–1); West Coast last (1–22).
- Each club played 23 H&A games; league premiership points total 828 per season
  (207 H&A matches × 4), the expected invariant.

## Notes

- `club_match.drv_premiership_points` left untouched (vestigial; points live on
  club_season) — same as 1998–2023.
- The finals-exclusion gap in `domain.CalculateLadder` /`FindFinalBySeasonID`
  (filters on `data_status='final'`, not round type) still stands: with
  2024/2025 finals now `final`, the Go ladder path would wrongly include them.
  The SQL here excludes finals correctly; the app path needs the same fix before
  it recomputes these seasons' ladders.
